==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈməʊɡ(ə)l/|/ˈmoʊɡəl/|n2={{R:Lexico}}}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mogul.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Etymology 1===
Figurative use of {{m|en|Moghul}}, which originally meant [[Mongol]], or person of Mongolian descent. In this context, it refers to the [[Mughal Empire]] (mughal being Persian or Arabic for "Mongol") of the Indian Subcontinent that existed between 1526 and 1857: the early Mughal emperors claimed a heritage dating back to the Mongol ruler [[Genghis Khan]]. The modern meaning of the word is supposedly derived from the storied riches of the Mughal emperors, which, for example, produced the [[Taj Mahal]].

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[rich]] or [[powerful]] person; a [[magnate]].
#: {{syn|en|magnate|tycoon|captain of industry}}
#: {{ux|en|a Silicon Valley tech '''mogul'''}}

